Documentation housekeeping (`#89 <https://github.com/sandialabs/PEAT/issues/89>`_):

- ``CONTRIBUTING.rst`` is now the single contribution guide; the out-of-sync ``.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`` was removed and its unique content (commit message format, rebase and force-push commands, review requests, license note) merged in. The guide now documents that Conventional Commits types MUST be lowercase for both commit messages and PR titles, and the Versioning and Release process sections match the current ``workflow_dispatch``-based release workflow.
- The documentation published to GitHub Pages is rebuilt when a release is created, so it no longer shows the previous release's version.
- ``docs/dependencies_table.rst`` is generated during the docs build (``pdm run docs-html`` / ``docs-man`` run ``dep-doc`` first) instead of being committed and going stale.
- The reference documents page was renamed from ``module_documents`` to ``reference_documents``, the device module documents are a visible "Device module documents" section, and the CLI usage reference sub-sections are now part of the table of contents, so section numbering is correct.
- OpenPLC Runtime v4 module docs: ``default_options`` is a Python code block matching the module, the HTTP example is a real request line, and ``plugins_to_query`` is documented as a mapping of plugin name to command.
- Fixed stale or broken content found in a review pass: wrong CLI flags (``--pcap``, ``--rundir``), missing subcommands in the operate overview, references to nonexistent classes, config options, constants, and example paths, invalid YAML in the ``device_options`` example, incorrect default file paths, supported Python and Ubuntu versions, ruff line length and ``noqa`` codes, and reStructuredText markup that rendered incorrectly.
